From: Vendomat Fork <vendomat-fork@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] vendomat: copy a lazily mounted locked source into the
 store

Patch 0003 (PR #3244) reuses a locked source when its store path
exists, and marks the path as a store dependency with appendContext.
The in-process locker can mount a fetched source at that path without
registering it. `builtins.pathExists` is then true, but the store lacks
the path, and the shell fails with "path ... is required, but there is
no substituter that can build it". This happens on the first entry of
any workspace whose git sources are not yet in the store.

Produce the path with `builtins.path` and the locked narHash. Nix
copies a mounted tree into the store with the expected hash, and
returns a registered path without reading it.

Upstream: fork-only. It corrects patch 0003 under lazy trees; report it
on cachix/devenv PR #3244.
---
 devenv-nix-backend/bootstrap/resolve-lock.nix | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/devenv-nix-backend/bootstrap/resolve-lock.nix b/devenv-nix-backend/bootstrap/resolve-lock.nix
index bcf9c68c..d7a00515 100644
--- a/devenv-nix-backend/bootstrap/resolve-lock.nix
+++ b/devenv-nix-backend/bootstrap/resolve-lock.nix
@@ -117,7 +117,15 @@ let
                 revCount = null;
               } locked
               // {
-                outPath = builtins.appendContext storedPath { ${storedPath}.path = true; };
+                # The in-process locker can mount a fetched source at this path without
+                # registering it, so pathExists is true while the store lacks the path.
+                # builtins.path with the locked hash copies such a tree into the store, and
+                # returns a registered path unchanged.
+                outPath = builtins.path {
+                  path = storedPath;
+                  name = "source";
+                  sha256 = locked.narHash;
+                };
               }
               // (
                 if locked ? lastModified then
